From 9ceaec66f489802523deb967584a974ecdc7d6e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:08:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 276/350] Unified: two picks are measured on the bar right
 away; hovering a tool previews its result

The bar next to a pick shows, on its left, what one or two picked things measure without
pressing "Measure": point to point (with dX/dY/dZ), point to face or edge, the gap of
parallel edges or faces and the angle of the others, diameters and the distance of the
centers of circles and holes, the length of one edge and the area of one face. A click
copies a number; "Keep the dimension" makes a Measure object (one undo step). The tools
stay on the right, the two-pick tools of 0.5.8 included.

Resting the mouse on a tool of the tool strip or of the bar (300 ms) shows a see-through
ghost of what it would do on the picked things: the corners a fillet or chamfer takes off,
the block an extrusion adds or a pocket cuts, the hole, the mirrored or repeated feature.
It is worked out on copies in a thread, cancelled when the mouse leaves, dropped when it
takes over a second; the document is never changed. The tools get a tooltip of one plain
sentence.

MeasureMath.py / ToolPreview.py without the GUI ("FreeCADCmd -t TestMeasureMath",
"-t TestToolPreview"), MeasureBarGui.py / ToolPreviewGui.py with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
